KA. Manual therapy for the pediatric population: a systematic review. BMC Complement Altern Med. 2019;19(1):60. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Driehuis F, Hoogeboom TJ, Nijhuis-van der Sanden MWG, de Bie RA, Staal JB. Spinal manual therapy in infants, children and adolescents: a systematic review and meta-analysis on treatment indication, technique and outcomes. PLoS ONE. 2019;14(6):e0218940. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Gleberzon BJ, Arts J, Mei A, McManus EA. The use of spinal manipulative therapy for pediatric health conditions: a systematic review of the literature. J Can Chiropr Assoc. 2012;56(2):128-141. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Hawk C, Schneider MJ, Vallone S, Hewitt EG. Best practices for chiropractic care of children: a consensus update. J Manipulative Physiol Ther. 2016;39(3):158-168. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Balon JAP, Crowther ER, Danielson C, et al. A comparison of active and simulated chiropractic manipulation as adjunctive treatment for childhood asthma. N Engl J Med. 1998;339:1013-1020. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Bronfort G, Evans RL, Kubic P, Filkin P. Chronic pediatric asthma and chiropractic spinal manipulation: a prospective clinical series and randomized clinical pilot study. J Manip Physiol Ther. 2001;24:369-377. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Kaminskyj A, Frazier M, Johnstone K, Gleberzon BJ. Chiropractic care for patients with asthma: a systematic review of the literature. J Can Chiropr Assoc. 2010;54(1):24-32. [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Karpouzis F, Bonello R, Pollard H. Chiropractic care for paediatric and adolescent attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder: a systematic review. Chiropr Osteopat. 2010;18:13. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Amjad I, Niazi IK, Kumari N, et al. The effects of chiropractic adjustment on inattention, hyperactivity, and impulsivity in children with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder: a pilot RCT. Front Psychol. 2024;15:1323397. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Chiropractic and autism: everything you should know. Harlan Chiropractic & Acupuncture. Accessed October 2, 2024. https://www.drchrisharlan.com/chiropractic-and-autism-everything-you-should-know/ 29. Alcantara J, Alcantara JD, Alcantara J. A systematic review of the literature on chiropractic care of patients with autism spectrum disorder. Explore (NY). 2011;7(6):384-390. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Alcantara J, Alcantara JD, Alcantara J. The chiropractic care of infants with breastfeeding difficulties. Explore (NY). 2015;11(6):468-474. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 31. Dobson D, Lucassen PLBJ, Miller JJ, Vlieger AM, Prescott P, Lewith G. Manipulative therapies for infantile colic. Cochrane Database Syst Rev. 2012;12:CD004796. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Holm LV, Jarbøl DE, Christensen HW, Søndergaard J, Hestbæk L. The effect of chiropractic care on infantile colic: results from a single-blind randomised controlled trial. Chiropr Man Therap. 2021;29(1):15. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Lynge S, Dissing KB, Vach W, Christensen HW, Hestbaek L. Effectiveness of chiropractic manipulation versus sham manipulation for recurrent headaches in children aged 7–14 years—a randomised clinical trial. Chiropr Man Therap. 2021;29(1):1. doi: 10.1186/s12998-020-00360-3. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Manansala C, Passmore S, Pohlman K, Toth A, Olin G. Change in young people’s spine pain following chiropractic care at a publicly funded healthcare facility in Canada. Complement Ther Clin Pract. 2019;35:301-307. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Vasaghi-Gharamaleki B, Naser Z. Predicting the risk of hearing impairment following the cervical spine diseases by measuring the cervical